00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:24,060
Is that alcohol?

251
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:27,817
My harvest can get its hands on
anything I order it to snatch.

252
00:14:27,900 --> 00:14:32,040
So, I had to grab some booze when
we ran past the liquor store.

253
00:14:32,380 --> 00:14:33,937
And when you weren't paying attention,

254
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:37,020
I injected the hooch into
your stupid lying bodies.

255
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:40,497
Well, to be more specific, I made
it squirt right into your veins.

256
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:41,500
Wait, you what?

257
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:45,560
Aw, get out!

258
00:14:46,900 --> 00:14:49,371
When alcohol goes directly into the veins,

259
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:52,617
you don't need that much until
you're shit-faced and flailing.

260
00:14:52,700 --> 00:14:55,497
I knew alcohol could be used
as a makeshift anesthetic,

261
00:14:55,580 --> 00:14:57,337
but I never thought a kid
would figure that out?

262
00:14:57,420 --> 00:14:59,773
let alone use it to whammy me like this.

263
00:14:59,900 --> 00:15:02,488
Looks like he's not a
total idiot after all.

264
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:05,620
No, it must be his instinct again.

265
00:15:06,160 --> 00:15:07,840
Oh, he's dead meat.

266
00:15:08,520 --> 00:15:13,402
I might be a little tipsy, but there's no
way that's gonna stop me from ending you.

267
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:19,960
My frickin' eye!

268
00:15:20,480 --> 00:15:23,260
What are you waiting for, Josuke? Fix it!

269
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:24,597
Shit, hang in there!

270
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:25,510
I'm on it!

271
00:15:25,593 --> 00:15:27,633
If I'm remembering everything correctly,

272
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:31,997
you two dickwads called me a whole bunch
of shitty names earlier, didn't you?

273
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:34,417
I'm gonna show you what
happens when you try to pull

274
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:37,500
the wool over my eyes and
treat me like a dumb kid.

275
00:15:37,940 --> 00:15:38,770
Damn you!

276
00:15:39,420 --> 00:15:41,517
You're standing there
all high and mighty when

277
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:44,017
you breaking your promise
is what started this!

278
00:15:44,100 --> 00:15:45,940
I've had about all I can take.

279
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:49,417
Keep this up and you're not
gonna like what comes next.

280
00:15:49,500 --> 00:15:52,997
I think you've done more than enough
talking for one life, jerks gay.

281
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:57,137
And since your stand's weak, your bite
can't even back up your puny bark.

282
00:15:57,220 --> 00:15:59,217
Actually, both of your stands are shit,

283
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:02,117
so save the demands until you're
half as strong as Harvest.

284
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:03,917
Till then, take it in the eye.

285
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:05,765
Quick, Josuke, close your eye!

286
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:08,320
You okay?

287
00:16:08,980 --> 00:16:10,540
Damn. So close.

288
00:16:10,900 --> 00:16:13,460
There's no point in
closing your eyes, FYI.

289
00:16:13,680 --> 00:16:16,557
Harvest can grab anything,
no matter the obstacle.

290
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:18,837
Shut those peepers as tight as you want.

291
00:16:18,920 --> 00:16:22,155
It'll just tear off your
eyelids and gouge out the eye.

292
00:16:23,320 --> 00:16:25,760
We get the point, Shigechi. Stop it.

293
00:16:25,940 --> 00:16:27,352
Just forgive us already.

294
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:29,297
It's not like we wanted this to happen.

295
00:16:29,380 --> 00:16:30,210
Huh?

296
00:16:30,293 --> 00:16:31,123
Was that an apology?

297
00:16:31,420 --> 00:16:32,280
Damn it, kid.

298
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:34,597
I have had it with your shitty attitude.

299
00:16:34,680 --> 00:16:35,797
Hear that, Okuyasu?

300
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:38,637
Josuke seems to be on a completely
different page from you.

301
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:39,550
Don't worry about him.

302
00:16:39,633 --> 00:16:40,619
He'll come around.

303
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:43,424
But how about we give you this?

304
00:16:44,640 --> 00:16:49,017
It's the 10,000 yen you gave me, plus
everything else I have on me right now.

305
00:16:49,100 --> 00:16:51,537
Take it as our penance for
all the trouble we've caused.

306
00:16:51,620 --> 00:16:54,317
Police Shigechi, I'm begging
you not to off Josuke.

307
00:16:54,400 --> 00:16:56,753
If he gets taken out, who'll fix my eye?

308
00:16:57,140 --> 00:16:58,140
Oh, Okuyasu!

309
00:16:59,060 --> 00:17:00,220
Huh? Oh, yeah.

310
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:03,485
I almost forgot I gave
you that little handout.

311
00:17:03,760 --> 00:17:05,642
I felt so bad for you beta boys,

312
00:17:05,780 --> 00:17:09,657
I decided the only right thing to do
was bless you with over 10,000 yen.

313
00:17:09,740 --> 00:17:11,357
Here, the money's all yours.

314
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:14,620
Just have mercy on us,
old strong one! I...

315
00:17:19,460 --> 00:17:20,820
Way to use your brain.

316
00:17:21,120 --> 00:17:24,397
You're trying to lure him in like
catching a raccoon with a bit of bait.

317
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:27,833
Once he closes the distance,
bam, you'll let him have it.

318
00:17:28,260 --> 00:17:30,057
Well, I've got your back, buddy.

319
00:17:30,140 --> 00:17:32,320
Go for it, man, work your magic.

320
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:34,020
That's a good boy.

321
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:36,977
I don't know where this newfound
obedience is coming from,

322
00:17:37,060 --> 00:17:39,413
but I'm glad you know the pecking order.

323
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:46,400
Something wonky's going on.

324
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:47,860
Hey now, Okuyasu,

325
00:17:48,180 --> 00:17:50,037
it feels like you're trying to lure me in

326
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:52,397
with cash so you can
attack me with your stand.

327
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:54,737
But you wouldn't do
that, would you, old pal?

328
00:17:54,820 --> 00:17:55,650
No.

329
00:17:55,780 --> 00:17:57,800
So you were trying to trick me.

330
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:03,340
Did you think I'd honestly fall for a
harebrained scheme as lame as that one?

331
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:06,275
You must think I'm some kind of idiot.

332
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:08,120
Well, no pity for you.

333
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:11,040
It's not like we needed it anyway.

334
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:13,297
Time's run out for you, little man.

335
00:18:13,380 --> 00:18:16,437
I guess you were too busy
flapping your gums like a dumbass

336
00:18:16,520 --> 00:18:20,167
to realize that you walked right
into the hand-striking range.

337
00:18:20,780 --> 00:18:23,077
I'll claw away the air
and make a teleport,

338
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:26,219
forcing the ticket out of
your hands and back to us.

339
00:18:26,380 --> 00:18:27,740
This ticket is ours.

340
00:18:28,140 --> 00:18:29,700
It belongs with you.

341
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,824
You know who you're talking to.

342
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:36,197
Idiots, you wasted your time
because I'm about to take it back.

343
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:38,537
Incredible, you're even
dumber than I thought.

344
00:18:38,620 --> 00:18:41,637
Your chance of winning just expired
and you never saw it coming.

345
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:42,920
My money!

346
00:18:43,360 --> 00:18:45,357
What do you think you're
doing to that ticket?

347
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:48,837
It's worth five million yen and
you're ripping it up like it's trash!

348
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:50,214
Why would you do that?

349
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:51,797
I don't get you in the least!

350
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:54,117
What was the point in going
through all this hoopla if you

351
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:56,577
were just going to rip it up
when you finally got your way?

352
00:18:56,660 --> 00:19:00,837
Because of you, I needed a surefire way
to stop you from attacking us again.

353
00:19:00,920 --> 00:19:03,697
Since you can't restore the
ticket without my shining diamond,

354
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:05,337
giving up is your best bet.

355
00:19:05,420 --> 00:19:06,420
The fight's over.

356
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:07,991
Accept it and stand down.

357
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:09,700
Oh, I get it now.

358
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:10,857
That's what you're doing.

359
00:19:10,940 --> 00:19:12,200
And off they go.

360
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:14,980
Your victory's blowing away in the wind.

361
00:19:15,220 --> 00:19:16,050
I take it all back.

362
00:19:16,133 --> 00:19:17,117
I don't get any of this.

363
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:19,377
Why would you throw
away five million again?

364
00:19:19,460 --> 00:19:20,940
Have you lost your mind?

365
00:19:21,280 --> 00:19:23,980
Harvest, bring back every last piece. Go!

366
00:19:27,100 --> 00:19:29,820
Holy shit, you really
don't get it, do you?

367
00:19:30,400 --> 00:19:34,341
Sending Harvest on a fetch quest
was the final nail in your coffin.

368
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:39,657
Your last line of defense is running
through the city looking for paper scraps.

369
00:19:39,740 --> 00:19:42,681
so who's gonna protect you
from these drunks, huh?

370
00:19:42,800 --> 00:19:44,600
I think I get it now.

371
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:50,600
We did it.

372
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:53,972
Since I caught you lying down on the job,

373
00:19:54,280 --> 00:19:57,104
why don't we try and get
in a bit of study time?

374
00:19:57,320 --> 00:20:01,057
The scraps of paper floating around
town are picked up by your harvest.

375
00:20:01,140 --> 00:20:04,669
But after that, who has the
power to put them back together?

376
00:20:04,940 --> 00:20:05,770
Hmm?

377
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:06,880
I need an answer.

378
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:10,317
Who can put the scraps back
together with Shining Diamond.

379
00:20:10,400 --> 00:20:12,740
You, Josuke. Josuke?

380
00:20:12,940 --> 00:20:15,117
Sounds to me like you're
forgetting something.

381
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:16,030
Yes, Mr.

382
00:20:16,113 --> 00:20:16,943
Josuke, sir.

383
00:20:17,180 --> 00:20:19,057
Ah, now that's what I like to hear.

384
00:20:19,140 --> 00:20:23,077
And I'm sure you know the name of the
person who recovered that IOU from you.

385
00:20:23,160 --> 00:20:25,300
Well, say his name, Half-Pint.

386
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:27,880
It's Okuyasu, the Great.

387
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:30,000
Good, that's our special man.

388
00:20:30,360 --> 00:20:33,637
So, what do you say we change
subjects and do a little math?

389
00:20:33,720 --> 00:20:36,377
How do we split five million
between three people?

390
00:20:36,460 --> 00:20:40,284
And remember, everyone has to be
happy when all is said and done.

391
00:20:40,880 --> 00:20:43,320
Well, I'm fine with half. Half, huh?

392
00:20:43,760 --> 00:20:46,997
Did I or did I not just tell you
there are three of us to consider?

393
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:49,997
How are each of us supposed to
get half the winnings, Shigechi?

394
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:53,962
Good thing we're studying because
your math needs some work, dude.

395
00:20:55,100 --> 00:20:55,980
Anyone home?

396
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:01,820
I guess I'll be okay with a third.

397
00:21:03,600 --> 00:21:08,365
Now that I think about it, without your
help, I'd still be collecting old stamps.

398
00:21:08,600 --> 00:21:11,000
I was acting like a spoiled brat.

399
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:14,616
We all found that lottery
ticket by working as a team.

400
00:21:14,880 --> 00:21:18,645
If we hadn't banded together, we
never would have pulled it off.

401
00:21:19,080 --> 00:21:21,280
Wow, it's starting to make sense.

402
00:21:21,920 --> 00:21:24,740
My greed kept me from
seeing the big picture.

403
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:28,882
Let's split everything fair and
square so we all get what we want.

404
00:21:31,340 --> 00:21:32,460
There we go!

405
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:34,776
I've never seen so much money before!

406
00:21:35,020 --> 00:21:35,850
Five million yen!

407
00:21:35,933 --> 00:21:38,857
If you're interested in a home
for your newly acquired wealth,

408
00:21:38,940 --> 00:21:41,457
your funds would be very
secure at Budogaoka Bank.

409
00:21:41,540 --> 00:21:42,797
You bet we're interested!

410
00:21:42,880 --> 00:21:44,120
We finally did it!

411
00:21:44,280 --> 00:21:45,633
It's like I'm dreaming!

412
00:21:46,100 --> 00:21:47,160
I have a question.

413
00:21:47,320 --> 00:21:50,967
Didn't we agree to split the
winnings between the three of us?

414
00:21:51,100 --> 00:21:52,100
Hear me out.

415
00:21:52,280 --> 00:21:56,177
In the interest of maintaining a fair
and just agreement between us partners,

416
00:21:56,260 --> 00:21:59,457
wouldn't it be best to include
our stands in this deal?

417
00:21:59,540 --> 00:22:01,560
I mean, fair is fair, after all.

418
00:22:01,720 --> 00:22:04,817
And since Harvest is made
up of about 500 mini-stands,

419
00:22:04,900 --> 00:22:08,060
we should split the pot
five hundred to one to one.

420
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:11,200
That's not an issue, is it? Uh-huh!

421
00:22:11,500 --> 00:22:12,657
You're unbelievable!

422
00:22:12,740 --> 00:22:16,237
I thought you learned your lesson, but
you just don't know when to stop haggling,

423
00:22:16,320 --> 00:22:17,150
do you?

424
00:22:17,233 --> 00:22:19,289
I was only messing
around, a third is fine.

425
00:22:20,160 --> 00:22:23,866
For some, that's far too much
money for high schoolers to have.

426
00:22:23,960 --> 00:22:25,180
But c 'est la vie.

427
00:23:05,493 --> 00:23:06,417
To the arms and the lips and the face.

428
00:23:06,500 --> 00:23:08,417
Of the humic and of all that I need to.

429
00:23:08,500 --> 00:23:11,177
I want to come and stand
a little bit closer.

430
00:23:11,260 --> 00:23:13,457
Breathe in and get a bit higher.

431
00:23:13,540 --> 00:23:15,597
You'll never know what hit you!

432
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:17,957
When I get to you.

433
00:23:18,040 --> 00:23:19,797
Ooh, I want you.

434
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:22,320
I don't know if I need you.

435
00:23:23,120 --> 00:23:24,177
Ooh, I got it.

436
00:23:24,260 --> 00:23:25,380
If I know.

437
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:28,837
Ooh, I want you.

438
00:23:28,920 --> 00:23:31,260
I don't know if I need you.

439
00:23:32,040 --> 00:23:33,357
Ooh, I got it.

440
00:23:33,440 --> 00:23:34,297
If I know.
